                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(c,c') \to Hom_C(d,d')
                that sends
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ↦
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi c
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi q
                              %mtd
                                %mi c
                                %mo ′
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi g
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi d
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi d
                                %mo ′
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (q : c \stackrel{}{\to} c')
                      \\;\;\;
                      \\mapsto
                      \\;\;\,
                      \\left(
                      g \circ q \circ f \; : \;
                      \\array{
                      c &amp;\stackrel{q}{\to}&amp; c'
                      \\\
                      \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                      \\\
                      d &amp;&amp; d'
                      }
                      \\right)
                      \\,.
          .query
            %p
              Note: when the symbol
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
              is used, it denotes traditional right-to-left order of composition. For those who prefer the left-to-right order, the symbol
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ;
              may be used in place of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∘
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/discussion/7239/realigned-arrows-for-clarification-and-fixed-composition-order/"} here
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+hom-functor"} enriched hom-functor
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C(-,-) : C^{op} \times C \to V
          %p
            that sends objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c,c' \in C
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(c,c') \in V
          %p
            Some categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are equipped with an operation that behaves like a hom-functor, but takes values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            itself
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [-,-] : C^{op} \times C \to C
                  \\,.
          %p
            Such an operation is called an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            functor, and categories carrying this are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+categories"} closed categories
          %h3#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Note: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
            calls a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            a “precategory” and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            a “category”, but here we shall refer to the standard terminology of “category” and “univalent category” respectively.
          %p
            For any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "italic"}
                    %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_A : A^{op} \times A \to \mathit{Set}
          %p
            It takes a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≡
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b):(A^{op})_0 \times A_0 \equiv A_0\times A_0
            to the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_A(a,b)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mi op
                        %mo ×
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,f') : hom_{A^{op} \times A}((a,b),(a',b'))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:hom_A(a',a)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f': hom_A(b,b')
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (hom_A)_{(a,b),(a',b')}(f,f') \equiv (g\mapsto f' g f) : hom_A(a,b) \to hom_A(a',b')
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#representable_functors Representable functors
          %p
            Given a hom-functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom:C^{op}\times C\to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            one obtains a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h^c: C \to Set
          %p
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^c\coloneqq hom(c,-)
            and a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h_c : C^{op} \to Set
          %p
            given by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi c
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_c\coloneqq hom(-,c)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom: C^{op} \times C \to Set
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p Formally this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom(c,-) : C \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} * \times C  \stackrel{(c,Id)}{\to} C^{op} \times C \stackrel{hom(-,-)}{\to} Set
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Id
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom(-,c) : C \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} C^{op} \times *  \stackrel{(Id,c)}{\to} C^{op} \times C \stackrel{hom(-,-)}{\to} Set
                  \\,.
          %p
            Functors of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op} \to Set
            are called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(-,c)
            are called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            or
            %strong representable presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Functors of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to Set
            are called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copresheaves"} copresheaves
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(c,-)
            are called co
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            or
            %strong representable copresheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#preservation_of_limits Preservation of limits
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor+preserves+limits"} hom-functor preserves limits
            in both arguments separately. This means:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for fixed object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
                the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(c,-) : C \to Set
                sends limit
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                to limit diagrams in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                for fixed object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c' \in C
                the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(-,c') : C^{op} \to Set
                sends limit diagrams in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
                – which are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
                in
                = succeed "!" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p For instance for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi x
                          %mi z
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  y \times_x z &amp;\to&amp; y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  z &amp;\to&amp; x
                  }
          %p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
            any object, the induced diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Hom
                                %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo ,
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi x
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Hom_C(c,y) \times_{Hom_C(c,x)} Hom_C(c,z)\simeq &amp; Hom_C(c,y \times_x z)  &amp;\to&amp; Hom_C(c,y)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp; Hom_C(c,z) &amp;\to&amp; Hom_C(c,x)
                  }
          %p
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is again a pullback diagram. A moment of reflection shows that this statement is
            %em equivalent
            to the very definition of limit.
          %h3#relation_to_profunctors Relation to profunctors
          %p
            The hom-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom : C^{op}\times C\to Set
            is also the identity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_C: C &amp;#8696; C
          %p
            One way to see this is to notice that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C \to [C^{op}, Set]
          %p
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            in the 1-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            is the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi id
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C \stackrel{id}{\to} C \stackrel{j}{\to} [C^{op}, Set]
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{F} : C^{op} \times C \to Set
            whose hom-adjunct is of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \stackrel{F}{\to} C \stackrel{j}{\to} [C^{op}, Set]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            an ordinary functor are those in the inclusion of these ordinary functors into profunctors. So the hom-functor is the image of the identity functor under this inclusion.
